item.description:
Rising inflation, tariffs, and anti-incumbent backlash are shaking up traditional party strongholds across key Senate and House battlegrounds ahead of the midterm elections. While many believe the cycle favors Democrats this year, questions remain about whether they can deliver on bold campaign promises even if they take control of the House and the Senate. FOX News Senior Congressional Correspondent Chad Pergram joins to break down surprisingly tight contests in states like Kansas, Michigan, and South Carolina and the internal ideological rift awaiting a potential Democratic majority—detailing the clash between progressive demands for cabinet impeachments and the practical constraints faced by moderate swing-district lawmakers.Plus, Oklahoma Senator James Lankford joins to analyze how soaring diesel costs, domestic refining limits, and conflicts in Ukraine and Iran are affecting consumer prices, while warning that a Democratic Senate win could lead to gridlock and stalled judicial nominees.

PHOTO CREDIT: AP PHOTO&nbsp;


